1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 { This is the Ponziani Opening, one of the oldest chess openings. White just wants to build a strong centre with d4, but of course we will try to stop it. } d5 { A logical continuation fighting for the centre. As we will see, some of the lines are quite sharp and forcing but these usually are objectively very good for us. } 4. d3 { Objectively that's not bad but it was hardly an idea to play this way with 3.c3. -KEY- } dxe4 5. dxe4 Qxd1+ 6. Kxd1 Nf6 7. Bd3 Nd7 { Planning ... Nc5 with an equal position but an easier game. That's kind of a reversed Philidor endgame. } 
